   "en": {
    "headline": "Moonshot AI launches Kimi K3.1 Pro, an open model that approaches Claude Opus 5.5 at coding",
    "summary_short": "Moonshot AI unveils Kimi K3.1 Pro, a 3-trillion-class model with a 1-million-token context, and will release its weights by November 4. In its tests it comes close to the best closed models.",
    "summary_long": "Kimi K3.1 Pro is a version of Kimi K3 with much more post-training through reinforcement learning. It is already on Kimi.ai, Kimi Work, Kimi Code and the API, alongside a Highspeed variant that is 2 to 3 times faster. The full weights will arrive by November 4. On Terminal-Bench 4.0, which measures coding agents in the terminal, it scores 65.7%: ahead of GPT-6 Astra (58.2%) and just behind Claude Opus 5.5 (66.4%). On BenchCAD, a 3D modeling test, it scores 92.7%, below Opus 5.5 (96.2%).\n\nThe company says it has cut hallucinations on a hard internal test from 23.4% to 8.3%. It also removed cybersecurity data from training so as not to release an open model with more offensive capability than the closed ones. Without that cleanup, it solved 90.5% of its exploit challenges; with it, 81%. All figures come from Moonshot, and several are from internal tests.",
    "unconfirmed_claims": [
     "The benchmark and hallucination figures are published by Moonshot AI; several come from internal tests.",
     "According to Moonshot AI, its offensive cybersecurity capability remains behind the leading closed models."
    ]
   },
